@@ -3,10 +3,11 @@ ClimaAtmos.jl Release Notes
 
 main
 ----
+- ![][badge-💥breaking] The energy source tags are now safe by default. **`energy_source_tags` without `energy_source_tag_offset` is refused at configuration time**, with the numbers a run needs to choose one; `energy_source_tag_offset: 0` keeps the tags on `ρe_tot` exactly as before. With a pure region tag, `energy_source_closure_check` now runs by default, once a day, and only reports: the family has no default `tolerance` any more (it was 1e-6) and `abort_above` stays off. The block gains `spin_up` (`1hours` by default, `~` for none), after which the check takes a reference residual, and `energy_source_tag_closure.csv` gains three columns, `residual_at_spin_up`, `residual_since_spin_up` and `relative_since_spin_up`, so anything parsing that file by column count needs updating. With `audit` on, `energy_source_tag_audit.csv` gains five columns: `source_negative`, `source_negative_relative`, `source_minimum`, `repair_moved` and `repair_moved_relative`. The repair's ledger `e_src_fix_<name>` joins the default output. At configuration time the tags now warn about a process that changes `ρe_tot` and that no tag follows, and about a `tracer_nonnegativity_method` whose clip changes `ρe_tot` outside every bracket. `config/model_configs/baroclinic_wave_energy_source_tags.yml` is a worked example.
 - ![][badge-✨feature/enhancement] The energy source tags now follow precipitation sedimentation under 1-moment and 2-moment microphysics. Sedimentation moves energy between levels, so the tags move with the falling water rather than being credited with new energy. Each face's energy flux, with `c` times the mass it carries under an offset, is shared out by the shares of the cell that loses the energy, which is the cell below where the water carries negative energy, as ice can. The partition tags' fluxes add up to the parent's exactly. It needs an `energy_source_tag_offset`, and warns without one. Under 0-moment microphysics nothing sediments and nothing changes.
 - ![][badge-✨feature/enhancement] The energy source tags and the process records now see precipitation on the implicit path. Under 0-moment microphysics, which is stepped implicitly by default, rain leaves the column through the implicit microphysics sink, and that sink is now bracketed for both families, as it already was for the water tags. The records also take precipitation sedimentation from the implicit path. The source tags do not, because sedimentation moves energy between levels and a bracket would count what arrives as new energy. The `ρe_tag_*` family is unchanged.
 - ![][badge-✨feature/enhancement] Add `energy_source_tag_repair`, on by default. Where the total they partition is positive, it keeps the energy source tags non-negative after each state update. The pure region tags keep their sum and give up a negative tag's deficit in proportion to what each holds, as the water tags' partition repair does, and a tag that carries a source is clipped at zero. Every change is logged in the new diagnostic `e_src_fix_<name>`. The repair does not force the tags onto the total, so `e_src_res` still shows the transport mismatch. `false` leaves the tags as the attribution rule and their transport make them, negative values included.
-- ![][badge-✨feature/enhancement] Add `energy_source_tag_offset`, an energy per kilogram of air that the energy source tags add to `ρe_tot` to form the total they partition, `ρe_tot + c·ρ`. The model never uses that total, so the simulated atmosphere is unchanged, while a large enough offset makes the total positive where `ρe_tot` is not and lets the donor rule run there. Moving the thermodynamic reference instead gives the tags the same total in exact arithmetic, but it reaches the model's numerics. The default, `~`, leaves the tags on `ρe_tot` exactly as before. See docs/src/energy_source_tags.md.
+- ![][badge-✨feature/enhancement] Add `energy_source_tag_offset`, an energy per kilogram of air that the energy source tags add to `ρe_tot` to form the total they partition, `ρe_tot + c·ρ`. The model never uses that total, so the simulated atmosphere is unchanged, while a large enough offset makes the total positive where `ρe_tot` is not and lets the donor rule run there. Moving the thermodynamic reference instead gives the tags the same total in exact arithmetic, but it reaches the model's numerics. An offset of `0` leaves the tags on `ρe_tot` exactly as before. See docs/src/energy_source_tags.md.
 - [#64](https://github.com/johannespletzer/ClimaAtmosResiDyn.jl/issues/64) ![][badge-🐛bugfix] Stop the water tags diverging while `ρq_tot` stays bounded. `rescale_water_tags!` followed a limiter or state constraint by multiplying every tag by `r = ρq_tot_after / ρq_tot_before`. Writing `e = ρq_tot - Σₖ ρq_tagₖ` for the closure error the `q_tag_res` diagnostic reports, that gave `e_after = r · e_before` in every cell with a positive parent — a no-op on the error only when the error was already zero. The SEM quasimonotone limiter's lower bound is the element minimum of `q` from the reference state, so a node sitting below it is lifted every stage with `r > 1`; on a sphere that compounded at about 1.4 per limiter application and reached a relative residual of 6e113 in 24 simulated hours, with tags at 1e130 against a `ρq_tot` that stayed inside 1.6185e16 to 1.6214e16. The run reported success.
   - The correction is now additive. The parent's increment `Δ = ρq_tot_after - ρq_tot_before` is handed to the tags under the donor rule the rest of the file already uses, `ρq_tagₖ += Δ · sₖ`, with `sₖ` renormalized over the partition so the shares sum to one. On a partition that is closed and non-negative this is the *same expression* as the old factor, so nothing changes for a well-behaved cell; the two differ only on `e`, which is exactly where multiplying was wrong. The new recursion is `e_after = e_before` wherever the partition holds water and the loss floor does not bind, and `e_after = e_before + min(Δ + Σₖ max(ρq_tagₖ, 0), 0)` where it does — bounded by `|Δ|`, never a multiple of `e_before`.
   - Non-negativity is preserved rather than restored, by the same mechanism as before: the loss the tags absorb is floored at what they hold, which on a closed partition reproduces the old ratio's floor at zero, so no non-negative tag is driven below zero. A tag that is already negative is not lifted by this correction — its share is zero — and waits for `repair_water_tag_partition!`, which is the correction that exists for it. A source tag keeps its own unnormalized donor share, floored at the parent, mirroring the split `sediment_water_tags!` already makes. The `ρq_tot_before ≤ 0` branch still empties every tag, for the reason its docstring gave. All of it is still recorded in `q_tag_fix_<name>` before it is applied.
